message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D transform */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ The card itself ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:160px;
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    background:#fff;
    transition:transform .6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;     /* keep children in 3D space */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* spin 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:#333;
    padding:20px;
    box-sizing:border-box;
}

.card-front {
    background:#e0f7fa;
}

.card-back {
    background:#ffebee;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* place back face opposite front */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | The page is centered with flexbox. |
| **2** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D context. |
| **3** | The card has a fixed size, rounded corners, shadow, and a transition for smooth animation. |
| **4** | On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **5** | Two faces (`front` and `back`) are absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the back face when it’s turned away from the viewer. The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so that it appears correctly after the card turns. |

You can replace the text inside `<p>` tags with images, icons, or any content you like.  
If you want a different rotation axis or angle, change the `transform:rotateY(180deg)` line accordingly. Enjoy!
